title Caravan refrain -- a named ending finally changes what the plan does next
prompt Keaton's standing autonomous loop: read the voice and style first, then the living card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, prove it on metal, and send it as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED -- %96, %97, %98, %99 each carry a proof line. No red books the allocation, so the constructive queue is open.
think The running thread is the correspondence arc in Caravan. The newest log's recommend names the door exactly: a run that has named an inherited ending should carry nobody about that matter again -- the one claim the respect rung's prose does not make and its code does not back.
think Read the shape rather than recall it. respect publishes twelve bytes into plan.respect and takes the inherited closure down, and then the very same run calls that person again, because carry_the_wall five tiers down runs on the plan's own word and nothing above it ever weighs the mark. Naming an ending changed what the outcome said and nothing about what the plan did.
think Named the rung refrain. Grepped the whole tree: zero occurrences in .rye and .rish, so no collision. spare was rejected on the lap below for a reason that still holds -- six rungs already spend spare with another sense.
think Modelled it on desist, which is the arc's own read-the-elder-mark shape: open the note a run before today published, weigh the word standing in the reader's own box rather than the one the plan is holding, publish the record, read it back, and only then act. Placed it ahead of respect_the_ending so it reads the elder mark before this run's own respecting writes over it -- exactly where bound_the_relay stands relative to mind_the_impasse.
think Made the consent guard read the person rather than the plan. RefrainTakenUp refuses where the reader's own box no longer ends the matter, so a correspondence they reopened since the ending was named stays live and the plan keeps answering them. Reading consent out of the mark the plan is holding would have been the plan consenting on the reader's behalf.
think Chose to take down the summons rather than to veto the beckoning. Every rung of this arc records and measures; none vetoes a rung below. So the act is the withdrawal of the call standing in the reader's box, and the record lands first -- a run falling between the two leaves a reader summoned rather than one spared with nothing saying why.
think Ran the pair on a wire where neither plan inherits a closure. The mark both plans act on is seated by the harness for a run before today, which is the only kind of mark this rung was ever meant to read -- and it leaves the respecting below reading 0 against 0 honestly rather than conveniently.
think Retailed six self-test reads rather than copying them. Under a refraining run the summons is gone by design, so the call bytes are read where they still stand and the box is read for the emptiness this rung caused. A copied read would have failed for the right reason and been repaired for the wrong one.
obs The measurement falls 1 to 0 -- readers a plan summoned again about a matter it had already named as ended. On the wire the record reads osrwsmwbyocrf: thirteen bytes carrying eight tiers, every byte save one from outside this run.
obs The carry did not move. Four births in a row have now left it at 47 lines against a ceiling of 4,000, and the ladder grew to 101 modules and 1,275 checks. Fold C's promise -- a rung costs the ladder only its own checks -- is now proven four times by doing.
obs The four bodies the last lap predicted would lift came due exactly on schedule. check_conclude_measure and check_conclude_wire were one body per rung until a rung was born above respect; born it was, they agreed, and both lifted whole beside check_respect and its refusals. check_respect_measure and check_respect_wire take the terminal seat in their place.
obs REDS %99's class did not recur, and the reason is mechanical rather than lucky. The lift transformer masks string and comment spans before it prefixes a single identifier, so the harness prose guard read OK over 398 comments and 970 literals on its first pull.
obs The 70-line ratchet fired on this rung's close_the_quarrel at 86 lines, and it is carried rather than answered. That function is the ladder's parity spine -- every rung's copy reads against the rung below it -- so splitting one rung's copy alone would cost the readable parallel the whole arc rests on. The split is right for the whole ladder at once, in its own round, and it is named here rather than rounded away.
obs Two planted controls, not one. The record was taken down and the closing read made again, failing on metal; and a summons was put back into the reader's box, making the read that closes the sparing claim fail there too. An act needs its own control, since a witness that only proves the record proves half the rung.
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=95 wall_s=323 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=yes
loom meter=caravan_ladder_copy carried_lines=47 prior=47 modules=101 checks=1275 fold_a=913 fold_b=85 fold_c_stubs=0
loom guard=caravan_ladder_harness_prose comments=398 literals=970 verdict=OK
loom rung=refrain measure=unspared_readers bare=1 under=0 record_bytes=13 tiers=8
file caravan/refrain.rye the rung -- a run that has named an ending calls that reader no further, and takes the summons back down
file tools/caravan_refrain_witness.rish the witness -- the measurement, the record on the wire, the empty box, and two planted controls
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye four bodies lifted: check_conclude_measure, check_conclude_wire, check_respect, check_respect_refusals
file caravan/respect.rye the four lifted bodies cut, so the harness answers for both rungs
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the refrain witness registered in the choir
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish fold pins moved to the measured 913 and 85
file caravan/README.md the rung's own section, the meter's numbers, and the terminal-seat paragraph that predicted this lift
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge refreshed to the refrain rung; the prior edge condensed to a pointer
recommend keep-going the correspondence arc is now whole in both directions and acts on what it learns: a plan stands a boundary, carries it to a person, hears them, moves on either word, writes the ending down, reads it back, and finally stops writing to a reader who is done. The next constructive door is the ladder's own orchestration -- close_the_quarrel has grown past seventy lines in every rung that holds it, and splitting it once for the whole ladder would answer the ratchet without costing the parity a reader follows. The carry stands at 47 against a ceiling of 4,000.
